{
  "esm": "2.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "ElementwiseAligned",
    "description": "An elementwise observed read at a cell whose array operands are aligned by index-set name (esm-spec \u00a74.3.4): w over [x, y] is c*q + k + r, with c over [x, y], q over [y] (the result's second axis, so aligning by leading position would read it at the wrong index), k over [x] (repeats along y) and r over [y, x] (the result's axes in the other order). The state c reads w at a cell, index(w, i, j), so the band calculus gathers each operand at the cell by name: index(q, j), index(k, i), index(r, j, i). Row c has bands on c (the diagonal), on q (column [j]) and on r (column [j, i]). The state s over [x, y] has the whole-array right-hand side -(s + q + r + 0.1*exp(q)), whose operands align with s the same way: row s has bands on s (the diagonal), on q (column [_r2], twice: the plain term and the exp term) and on r (column [_r2, _r1])."
  },
  "index_sets": {
    "x": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 3
    },
    "y": {
      "kind": "interval",
      "size": 2
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "Box": {
      "variables": {
        "c": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "x",
            "y"
          ],
          "default": 1.0
        },
        "q": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "shape": [
            "y"
          ],
          "default": 2.0
        },
        "r": {
